# Statistical Analysis of Literature: A Retrospective on &quot;Computers and the Humanities,&quot; 1966-1990.

**Authors:** Potter, Rosanne G.

## Abstract
Reviews essays on statistical analysis of literature from the journal &quot;Computers and the Humanities.&quot; Divides the essays into four groups: the philosophical, statistical analyses of language, literary texts, and themes. Questions whether valid statistical analysis of any text must be based on complete linguistic description. Emphasizes the importance of precomputational stages of learning about language. (DK)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ452250

